# Exact downstream request bytes, in order (step dividers)

### step 1: PUT http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/ws-auth (enable ws-auth via management)
PUT /v0/management/ws-auth HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 14


{"value":true}

### step 2: GET http://127.0.0.1:8397/v1/ws (no auth now required)
GET /v1/ws HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*




### step 3: GET http://127.0.0.1:8397/v1/ws (wrong key)
GET /v1/ws HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer wrong-key




### step 4: GET http://127.0.0.1:8397/v1/ws (valid key, upgrade still fails)
GET /v1/ws HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-local-key-1




### step 5: PUT http://127.0.0.1:8397/v0/management/ws-auth (disable ws-auth)
PUT /v0/management/ws-auth HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*
Authorization: Bearer oracle-mgmt-key-1
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 15


{"value":false}

### step 6: GET http://127.0.0.1:8397/v1/ws (no auth required again)
GET /v1/ws HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:8397
User-Agent: curl/8.7.1
Accept: */*



